    <folder name="Reference Library" id="id-e81f70cc41894e99ae56be41b5ee26ff">
      <folder name="TOGAF Artifact Guides" id="id-3b86339f26744e01bc6d9fad16bc13e6">
        <folder name="Preliminary Phase" id="id-83f6e4b85adf4b9180afa12ec500266c">
          <documentation>Guide views for the artifacts of the Preliminary Phase.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel" name="P-C01 Principles Catalog" id="id-bfc70b256f22493ebcd91d75af583a44">
            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-20864d8da28e4d8c8ffbde64d9068597" textAlignment="1" fillColor="#FFFFFF">
              <bounds x="24" y="24" width="620" height="400"/>
              <content>Principles Catalog
TOGAF catalog - Preliminary Phase

PURPOSE
Lists the business and architecture principles used to evaluate architecture decisions and to govern change initiatives.

MAIN ELEMENTS
Principle (with Driver, Goal, Outcome for context)

MAIN RELATIONSHIPS
Principle realizes Outcome, Outcome realizes Goal, Goal associated with Driver

HOW TO PRODUCE IN ARCHI
Produce the catalog from the model: list the elements of the types above with their name, documentation and properties (model tree filter, File > Export > Model to CSV, HTML report, or a jArchi script).

WHERE TO STORE THE RESULT
In the Landscape model: &quot;2 Architecture Landscape&quot; (2.1 Strategic, 2.2 Segment or 2.3 Capability Architectures), or &quot;3 Solution Landscape&quot; for Solution Building Blocks. Store exported catalogs, matrices and tables with the project deliverables.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Guide view for the TOGAF catalog &quot;Principles Catalog&quot; (Preliminary Phase).</documentation>
            <property key="TOGAF Artifact" value="Principles Catalog"/>
            <property key="ADM Phase" value="Preliminary Phase"/>
            <property key="Artifact Type" value="Catalog"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="(not a view: produced from the model)"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="TOGAF® Standard, 10th Edition - Architecture Content - https://pubs.opengroup.org/togaf-standard/architecture-content/chap03.html#tag_03_06_01_01"/>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Phase A - Architecture Vision" id="id-7fcd51d1e95f46d6b1bf2998485141d1">
          <documentation>Guide views for the artifacts (catalogs, matrices, tables and diagrams) of Phase A - Architecture Vision.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel" name="A-D01 Business Capability Map" id="id-82ada77407f64dc8b3b4b409afdea31b">
            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-b5c20f915fb1448fb8ffadd2a3227a42" textAlignment="1" fillColor="#FFFFFF">
              <bounds x="24" y="24" width="620" height="430"/>
              <content>Business Capability Map
TOGAF artifact - Phase A - Architecture Vision

PURPOSE
Shows the capabilities of the enterprise relevant to the architecture effort, structured hierarchically; a basis for heat maps of maturity, investment or scope.

ARCHIMATE VIEWPOINT
Capability Map

MAIN ELEMENTS
Capability, Resource, Outcome

MAIN RELATIONSHIPS
Composition, Aggregation, Assignment (Resource to Capability), Realization

TYPICAL STAKEHOLDERS
Executives, Business Architects

HOW TO USE
Use this guide as a reference. In the Landscape model, create the view in &quot;2 Architecture Landscape&quot; (2.1 Strategic, 2.2 Segment or 2.3 Capability Architectures), or in &quot;3 Solution Landscape&quot; (3.1, 3.2 or 3.3) when it describes Solution Building Blocks, name it after the artifact, copy the view properties (TOGAF Artifact, ADM Phase, ArchiMate Viewpoint), set the property &quot;Architecture State&quot; (Baseline, Transition or Target) and model the content.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Guide view for the TOGAF artifact &quot;Business Capability Map&quot; (Phase A - Architecture Vision).</documentation>
            <property key="TOGAF Artifact" value="Business Capability Map"/>
            <property key="ADM Phase" value="Phase A - Architecture Vision"/>
            <property key="Artifact Type" value="Diagram"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Capability Map"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="TOGAF® Standard, 10th Edition - Architecture Content, §3.6.3.5 - https://pubs.opengroup.org/togaf-standard/architecture-content/chap03.html#tag_03_06_02_05"/>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel" name="A-D02 Value Stream Map" id="id-6274e79dba9f42ac8f13061c6539a57b">
            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-43e63f55917b40459836aaebd64c7aad" textAlignment="1" fillColor="#FFFFFF">
              <bounds x="24" y="24" width="620" height="430"/>
              <content>Value Stream Map
TOGAF artifact - Phase A - Architecture Vision

PURPOSE
Shows how the enterprise creates value for a stakeholder as a sequence of value stages, and the capabilities that enable each stage.

ARCHIMATE VIEWPOINT
Value Stream

MAIN ELEMENTS
Value Stream (stages), Capability, Stakeholder, Value, Outcome

MAIN RELATIONSHIPS
Flow, Serving (Capability to Value Stream), Association

TYPICAL STAKEHOLDERS
Executives, Business Owners

HOW TO USE
Use this guide as a reference. In the Landscape model, create the view in &quot;2 Architecture Landscape&quot; (2.1 Strategic, 2.2 Segment or 2.3 Capability Architectures), or in &quot;3 Solution Landscape&quot; (3.1, 3.2 or 3.3) when it describes Solution Building Blocks, name it after the artifact, copy the view properties (TOGAF Artifact, ADM Phase, ArchiMate Viewpoint), set the property &quot;Architecture State&quot; (Baseline, Transition or Target) and model the content.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Guide view for the TOGAF artifact &quot;Value Stream Map&quot; (Phase A - Architecture Vision).</documentation>
            <property key="TOGAF Artifact" value="Value Stream Map"/>
            <property key="ADM Phase" value="Phase A - Architecture Vision"/>
            <property key="Artifact Type" value="Diagram"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Value Stream"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="TOGAF® Standard, 10th Edition - Architecture Content, §3.6.3.6 - https://pubs.opengroup.org/togaf-standard/architecture-content/chap03.html#tag_03_06_02_06"/>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel" name="A-D03 Value Chain Diagram" id="id-54393d8f633945b8ba8e28296ee88485">
            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-9ecc0a1d2179464da5e5312c6861a81d" textAlignment="1" fillColor="#FFFFFF">
              <bounds x="24" y="24" width="620" height="430"/>
              <content>Value Chain Diagram
TOGAF artifact - Phase A - Architecture Vision

PURPOSE
Gives a high-level orientation view of the enterprise and its interactions with the outside world (primary and support activities).

ARCHIMATE VIEWPOINT
Business Process Cooperation

MAIN ELEMENTS
Business Actor, Business Process, Business Function, Business Service

MAIN RELATIONSHIPS
Flow, Triggering, Serving

TYPICAL STAKEHOLDERS
Executives, Sponsors

HOW TO USE
Use this guide as a reference. In the Landscape model, create the view in &quot;2 Architecture Landscape&quot; (2.1 Strategic, 2.2 Segment or 2.3 Capability Architectures), or in &quot;3 Solution Landscape&quot; (3.1, 3.2 or 3.3) when it describes Solution Building Blocks, name it after the artifact, copy the view properties (TOGAF Artifact, ADM Phase, ArchiMate Viewpoint), set the property &quot;Architecture State&quot; (Baseline, Transition or Target) and model the content.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Guide view for the TOGAF artifact &quot;Value Chain Diagram&quot; (Phase A - Architecture Vision).</documentation>
            <property key="TOGAF Artifact" value="Value Chain Diagram"/>
            <property key="ADM Phase" value="Phase A - Architecture Vision"/>
            <property key="Artifact Type" value="Diagram"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Business Process Cooperation"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="TOGAF® Standard, 10th Edition - Architecture Content, §3.6.3.2 - https://pubs.opengroup.org/togaf-standard/architecture-content/chap03.html#tag_03_06_02_02"/>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel" name="A-D04 Solution Concept Diagram" id="id-4d50b7ebab3241c8b63b77ab3de05202">
            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-22ae116ed8684127865f151227978f17" textAlignment="1" fillColor="#FFFFFF">
              <bounds x="24" y="24" width="620" height="430"/>
              <content>Solution Concept Diagram
TOGAF artifact - Phase A - Architecture Vision

PURPOSE
Provides a high-level orientation of the solution envisaged to meet the goals of the architecture engagement.

ARCHIMATE VIEWPOINT
Strategy / Resource Map

MAIN ELEMENTS
Goal, Outcome, Course of Action, Capability, Resource, Value Stream

MAIN RELATIONSHIPS
Realization, Influence, Assignment

TYPICAL STAKEHOLDERS
Sponsor, Executives

HOW TO USE
Use this guide as a reference. In the Landscape model, create the view in &quot;2 Architecture Landscape&quot; (2.1 Strategic, 2.2 Segment or 2.3 Capability Architectures), or in &quot;3 Solution Landscape&quot; (3.1, 3.2 or 3.3) when it describes Solution Building Blocks, name it after the artifact, copy the view properties (TOGAF Artifact, ADM Phase, ArchiMate Viewpoint), set the property &quot;Architecture State&quot; (Baseline, Transition or Target) and model the content.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Guide view for the TOGAF artifact &quot;Solution Concept Diagram&quot; (Phase A - Architecture Vision).</documentation>
            <property key="TOGAF Artifact" value="Solution Concept Diagram"/>
            <property key="ADM Phase" value="Phase A - Architecture Vision"/>
            <property key="Artifact Type" value="Diagram"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Strategy / Resource Map"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="TOGAF® Standard, 10th Edition - Architecture Content, §3.6.3.3 - https://pubs.opengroup.org/togaf-standard/architecture-content/chap03.html#tag_03_06_02_03"/>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel" name="A-C01 Stakeholder Catalog" id="id-013b555fd04649d98bbea9cd110224ec">
            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-c18ed5d1a9da495aaaf46c2a5488b75b" textAlignment="1" fillColor="#FFFFFF">
              <bounds x="24" y="24" width="620" height="400"/>
              <content>Stakeholder Catalog
TOGAF catalog - Phase A - Architecture Vision

PURPOSE
Lists the stakeholders of the architecture engagement, their influence and their key concerns. Can also be drawn with the Stakeholder viewpoint.

MAIN ELEMENTS
Stakeholder, Driver, Assessment, Goal

MAIN RELATIONSHIPS
Stakeholder associated with Driver, Driver associated with Assessment and Goal

HOW TO PRODUCE IN ARCHI
Produce the catalog from the model: list the elements of the types above with their name, documentation and properties (model tree filter, File > Export > Model to CSV, HTML report, or a jArchi script).

WHERE TO STORE THE RESULT
In the Landscape model: &quot;2 Architecture Landscape&quot; (2.1 Strategic, 2.2 Segment or 2.3 Capability Architectures), or &quot;3 Solution Landscape&quot; for Solution Building Blocks. Store exported catalogs, matrices and tables with the project deliverables.</content>
            </child>
